event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":824,"item_id":"fc_03155c89c72fc7e7016ae22173ffb8819194c9266fe36bc7fa","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"version\":2,\"policy\":\"endpoint-fidelity-2\",\"source_inventory_sha256\":\"a9444478a4aff5832948fdbfe2e49f6d1fe8492674a3211f3fe98776212b9f61\",\"entries\":{\"P\":{\"selector\":\"decl:AuditBExport.P\",\"expected_type\":\"∀ (p : ℕ) (K : Type) [fieldK : Field K] (l : ℕ) (V : Type) [addV : AddCommGroup V] [modV : Module ℂ V] (x : Module.End ℂ V) (y : Module.End ℂ V) (h : Module.End ℂ V) (v : V) (M : Submodule ℤ V) (h_H001 : Nat.Prime p ∧ CharP K p ∧ l < p) (h_H002 : FiniteDimensional ℂ V ∧ Module.finrank ℂ V = l+1 ∧ h*x-x*h = (2 : ℂ) • x ∧ h*y-y*h = (-2 : ℂ) • y ∧ x*y-y*x = h ∧ (∀ W : Submodule ℂ V, LR.inv W x → LR.inv W y → LR.inv W h → W = ⊥ ∨ W = ⊤)) (h_H003 : v ≠ 0 ∧ x v = 0 ∧ h v = (l : ℂ) • v) (h_H004 : (∃ (ι : Type) (b : Module.Basis ι ℤ M) (c : Module.Basis ι ℂ V), ∀ i, (b i : V) = c i) ∧ (∀ r : ℕ, (∀ m : M, LR.divided x r m ∈ M) ∧ (∀ m : M, LR.divided y r m ∈ M))), ∃ A : LR.Actions M x y h, Nontrivial (LR.VK K M) ∧ ∀ W : Submodule K (LR.VK K M), LR.inv W (LR.induced K M A.lx.map) → LR.inv W (LR.induced K M A.ly.map) → LR.inv W (LR.induced K M A.lh.map) → W = ⊥ ∨ W = ⊤\",\"correspondence\":{\"mode\":\"equivalent\",\"explanation\":\"l ranges over naturals, identified bijectively with integers λ≥0; l<p is precisely the original bound. V, K, p, generators, highest vector and arbitrary M are universally parameterized. H002 encodes the complex Chevalley representation by its generators, dimension and irreducibility, and H003 supplies its nonzero highest-weight vector. An additive subgroup of V is uniquely an integer submodule, so H004 is exactly a shared integer/complex basis and stability under all divided powers; generator stability is equivalent to stability under their generated integer enveloping algebra. VK is K⊗Z M, identified with M⊗Z K by the canonical flip in both directions. Actions consists of restrictions to M with agreement in V; agreement determines each map uniquely because the inclusion M→V is injective. Existence is proved, not assumed (T014 constructs restrictions using H004 and h=xy-yx). Its induced maps act on pure tensors by k⊗m↦k⊗f(m), corresponding under the flip to m⊗k↦f(m)⊗k. Thus the existential choice of Actions neither weakens invariance nor adds a hypothesis: under H002,H004 restrictions exist and all choices coincide, so either formulation yields the other. Nontrivial is nonzeroness of the vector space, and bottom/top are zero/all subspaces. Invariance under x,y,h is equivalent to invariance under the abstract rank-three Chevalley Lie algebra: invariance under each generator implies invariance under every linear combination, and the reverse follows by specializing to generators. No faithfulness or distinct reduced weights, algebraic closure, p>2 or l>0 is imposed.\"}}},\"library_terms\":{}}}"}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":825,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_03155c89c72fc7e7016ae22173ffb8819194c9266fe36bc7fa","call_id":"call_9026246767e24f409e64f1edc28a43d5","name":"check_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"version\":2,\"policy\":\"endpoint-fidelity-2\",\"source_inventory_sha256\":\"a9444478a4aff5832948fdbfe2e49f6d1fe8492674a3211f3fe98776212b9f61\",\"entries\":{\"P\":{\"selector\":\"decl:AuditBExport.P\",\"expected_type\":\"∀ (p : ℕ) (K : Type) [fieldK : Field K] (l : ℕ) (V : Type) [addV : AddCommGroup V] [modV : Module ℂ V] (x : Module.End ℂ V) (y : Module.End ℂ V) (h : Module.End ℂ V) (v : V) (M : Submodule ℤ V) (h_H001 : Nat.Prime p ∧ CharP K p ∧ l < p) (h_H002 : FiniteDimensional ℂ V ∧ Module.finrank ℂ V = l+1 ∧ h*x-x*h = (2 : ℂ) • x ∧ h*y-y*h = (-2 : ℂ) • y ∧ x*y-y*x = h ∧ (∀ W : Submodule ℂ V, LR.inv W x → LR.inv W y → LR.inv W h → W = ⊥ ∨ W = ⊤)) (h_H003 : v ≠ 0 ∧ x v = 0 ∧ h v = (l : ℂ) • v) (h_H004 : (∃ (ι : Type) (b : Module.Basis ι ℤ M) (c : Module.Basis ι ℂ V), ∀ i, (b i : V) = c i) ∧ (∀ r : ℕ, (∀ m : M, LR.divided x r m ∈ M) ∧ (∀ m : M, LR.divided y r m ∈ M))), ∃ A : LR.Actions M x y h, Nontrivial (LR.VK K M) ∧ ∀ W : Submodule K (LR.VK K M), LR.inv W (LR.induced K M A.lx.map) → LR.inv W (LR.induced K M A.ly.map) → LR.inv W (LR.induced K M A.lh.map) → W = ⊥ ∨ W = ⊤\",\"correspondence\":{\"mode\":\"equivalent\",\"explanation\":\"l ranges over naturals, identified bijectively with integers λ≥0; l<p is precisely the original bound. V, K, p, generators, highest vector and arbitrary M are universally parameterized. H002 encodes the complex Chevalley representation by its generators, dimension and irreducibility, and H003 supplies its nonzero highest-weight vector. An additive subgroup of V is uniquely an integer submodule, so H004 is exactly a shared integer/complex basis and stability under all divided powers; generator stability is equivalent to stability under their generated integer enveloping algebra. VK is K⊗Z M, identified with M⊗Z K by the canonical flip in both directions. Actions consists of restrictions to M with agreement in V; agreement determines each map uniquely because the inclusion M→V is injective. Existence is proved, not assumed (T014 constructs restrictions using H004 and h=xy-yx). Its induced maps act on pure tensors by k⊗m↦k⊗f(m), corresponding under the flip to m⊗k↦f(m)⊗k. Thus the existential choice of Actions neither weakens invariance nor adds a hypothesis: under H002,H004 restrictions exist and all choices coincide, so either formulation yields the other. Nontrivial is nonzeroness of the vector space, and bottom/top are zero/all subspaces. Invariance under x,y,h is equivalent to invariance under the abstract rank-three Chevalley Lie algebra: invariance under each generator implies invariance under every linear combination, and the reverse follows by specializing to generators. No faithfulness or distinct reduced weights, algebraic closure, p>2 or l>0 is imposed.\"}}},\"library_terms\":{}}}","status":"completed"}}

